  "limits": "Queue counts are transport accounting, not a before/after Electron RAM result. The native UI workload ran during regression activity; no typing/interrupt latency distribution is claimed. Exact 4 MiB checksum parity uses a deliberately slow stand-in consumer; native xterm checks visible marker, flow window, hide/reload and interruption. A new renderer recovers its PTY and unacknowledged output, not previously parsed scrollback or terminal editor state. Sparse packet ceiling is independently tested with small configured limits. Legacy direct TerminalManager clients keep their synchronous event mode and do not gain this desktop ACK protocol. Packaged/macOS/Windows native measurements, aggregate budgets across many terminals and visited xterm/GPU/scrollback retention remain open."
